    {
      "title": "Divide by the new exponent",
      "body": "<p>For each power, increase its exponent by one and divide its coefficient by that new exponent. Keep the sign of the new exponent when doing the division.</p>",
      "recap": "The exponent increase and coefficient division are both required.",
      "pitfall": "The reciprocal term acquires a negative coefficient when integrated.",
      "pause": "Find your antiderivative, differentiate it to check both terms, and then evaluate the endpoints.",
      "recall": [
